# data-models-relationships

Core data model entities and relationships tracked in the bond compliance system:

## Primary Entities (Importance: 95/100)

1. Inmates/Defendants
- Central entity for tracking individuals under bond requirements
- Links to active cases, assigned agents, and compliance records
- Contains personal information and bond status

2. Bond Records
- Tracks bond amounts, conditions, and compliance requirements
- Associates defendants with specific location restrictions
- Maintains violation history and compliance status

3. Compliance Agents 
- Agency representatives managing defendant cases
- Permission levels and notification preferences
- Geographic jurisdiction assignments

## Key Relationships (Importance: 85/100)

- One-to-many relationship between Agents and Inmates
- Many-to-many between Locations and Bond Records
- One-to-many between Inmates and Compliance Events
- Direct linking between Bond Records and Location Restrictions

## Verification Records (Importance: 80/100)

- GPS check-in coordinates and timestamps
- Photo verification metadata
- SMS delivery confirmations
- Location compliance status updates
- Token validation history

## Geographic Data (Importance: 75/100)

- Approved location boundaries
- Check-in coordinates
- Jurisdiction zones
- Restricted areas
- VPN/proxy detection results

The data model prioritizes maintaining complete audit trails of all compliance-related activities while enabling real-time location verification and multi-factor authentication of check-ins.

